{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-hotelling-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-hotelling`, the Rates-scale twin of `process-crankcase-extidle`, `process-extended-idle` and `process-apu` together -- THC, CO and NOx from EXTENDED IDLE (90) and CRANKCASE EXTENDED IDLE (17), Atmospheric CO2 and Total Energy from extended idle, and Total Energy from the AUXILIARY POWER UNIT (91), which the calculator retags to SHORE POWER (93) for operating mode 203 -- for the diesel combination long-haul truck in Washtenaw County, road types 1 and 4, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. Hotelling is rated per hour and MOVES writes it to two tables `scale-rates` does not touch. RatePerHour is BaseRateOutput's emissionRate -- the inventory's adjusted rate over the cohort's source-bin share, per hotelling hour, crankcase extended idle chained from it -- and it is NOT a quotient: shore power's hours and inventory are zero here and its rate is not. RatePerVehicle is MOVESOutput over the cohort's population. Three source bins per cohort and two fuels (diesel and CNG) exercise the share and the regulatory class summed away. Measured in pandas against the three twins before the port: within 1e-05.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `process-crankcase-extidle`'s `n_sourceBin` and `n_physicsRow`, `n_ratesScale` = 1, and `n_outputRate` the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-hotelling"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-hotelling/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
